Q: BCryptSetProperty KDF to SHA256 fails for ECDH_P256 on Windows 25H2 26200.6584 and later A: <p>if look for <code>MSCryptEcDhSetProperty</code> implementation (which called from <code>BCryptSetProperty</code> on ECDH keys, code is look like</p>
<pre><code>#define BCRYPT_KEY_MAGIC        'MSKY'
#define BCRYPT_ALG_MAGIC       'MSAL'
#define BCRYPT_SECRET_MAGIC     'MSEC'


typedef struct BCRYPT_OBJECT_HEADER {
    ULONG cbSize;
    ULONG Magic;
} *PBCRYPT_OBJECT_HEADER;


#define WPP_LOG_ERROR(Status, Line) \
    if (WPP_GLOBAL_Control != &amp;WPP_GLOBAL_Control &amp;&amp; (WPP_GLOBAL_Control-&gt;Flags &amp; 1)) { \
        WPP_SF_sDsd(WPP_GLOBAL_Control-&gt;Logger, &quot;Status&quot;, \
        &quot;onecore\\ds\\security\\cryptoapi\\ncrypt\\msprim\\ecc\\ecc.c&quot;, Line, Status); \
    }

inline BOOLEAN ValidateEccHandle(_In_ PBCRYPT_OBJECT_HEADER hObject)
{
    if (!hObject || hObject-&gt;cbSize &lt; sizeof(BCRYPT_OBJECT_HEADER) + 4)
    {
        status = STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
        DebugTraceError(&quot;Status&quot;, &quot;onecore\\ds\\security\\cryptoapi\\ncrypt\\msprim\\ecc\\ecc.c&quot;, 438, status);
        WPP_LOG_ERROR(status, 438);
        return FALSE;
    }

    switch (hObject-&gt;Magic)
    {
    case BCRYPT_KEY_MAGIC:
    case BCRYPT_ALG_MAGIC:
        return TRUE;
    }

    status = STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE;
    DebugTraceError(&quot;Status&quot;, &quot;onecore\\ds\\security\\cryptoapi\\ncrypt\\msprim\\ecc\\ecc.c&quot;, 446, status);
    WPP_LOG_ERROR(status, 446);
    return FALSE;
}

NTSTATUS WINAPI MSCryptEcDhSetProperty(
    _In_ PBCRYPT_OBJECT_HEADER hObject,
    _In_ LPCWSTR pszProperty, 
    _In_reads_bytes_(cbInput) PUCHAR pbInput,
    _In_ ULONG cbInput, 
    _In_ ULONG dwFlags 
)
{
    NTSTATUS status;

    if (dwFlags) 
    {
        status = STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
        WPP_LOG_ERROR(status, 4017);
        return status;
    }

    if (!ValidateEccHandle(hObject))
    {
        status = STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
        WPP_LOG_ERROR(status, 4024);
        return status;
    }

    switch (hObject-&gt;Magic)
    {
    case BCRYPT_KEY_MAGIC:
        if (NT_SUCCESS(status = MSCryptEccSetKeyProperty(hObject, pszProperty, pbInput, cbInput, 0))) 
        {
            return STATUS_SUCCESS;
        }
        WPP_LOG_ERROR(status, 4041);
        return status;

    case BCRYPT_ALG_MAGIC:
        if (NT_SUCCESS(status = MSCryptEccSetAlgProperty(hObject, pszProperty, pbInput, cbInput, 0))) 
        {
            return STATUS_SUCCESS;
        }
        WPP_LOG_ERROR(status, 4054);
        return status;

    case BCRYPT_SECRET_MAGIC:
        if (NT_SUCCESS(status = MSCryptSetPropertySecret(hObject, pszProperty, pbInput, cbInput, 0))) 
        {
            return status;
        }
        WPP_LOG_ERROR(status, 4067);
        return status;
    }

    status = STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED;
    DebugTraceError(&quot;Status&quot;, &quot;onecore\\ds\\security\\cryptoapi\\ncrypt\\msprim\\ecc\\ecc.c&quot;, 4074, status);
    WPP_LOG_ERROR(status, 4074);
    return status;
}
</code></pre>
<p>code of <code>MSCryptEcDhSetProperty</code> is correct. this function handle 3 types of objects - ALG ( 'MSAL' ), KEY ( 'MSKY' ) and SECRET ('MSEC'). this function was in onecore\ds\security\cryptoapi\ncrypt\msprim\ecc\ecc.c file at lines 4000-4100 approximately. but at some moment, in begin of this function was inserted some validation function <code>ValidateEccHandle</code> - it was in the same file (ecc.c) but at lines 430-450 approximately. and this function containing bug - it forget about <code>BCRYPT_SECRET_MAGIC</code> case. as result when we try set any property on <code>BCRYPT_SECRET_HANDLE</code> we got error <code>STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE</code></p>

Q: Mudblazor Components custom CSS not loading A: <p>The reason your styles stop working when moved to a <code>.razor.css</code> file is CSS Isolation. Blazor adds a unique identifier (like <code>b-12345xyz</code>) to your component's HTML elements and the corresponding CSS rules to prevent styles from &quot;leaking&quot; to other components.</p>
<p>However, <strong>MudBlazor components</strong> (like <code>MudButton</code> or <code>MudDivider</code>) are rendered as child components. By default, CSS isolation only applies to HTML elements directly defined in your <code>.razor</code> file, not to the internal elements of child components.</p>
<p>To fix this, you need two things:</p>
<p><strong>1. Use the <code>::deep</code> Combinator</strong></p>
<p>The <code>::deep</code> selector tells Blazor to apply the style to any descendant element, even if it belongs to another component.</p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>/* Inside Component.razor.css */

::deep .rounded-pill {
    border-color: #b8d6ff !important;
}

::deep .rounded-pill .mud-divider {
    border-color: #b8d6ff !important;
}

::deep .appointments-tab-add-btn:hover {
    background: #e2f5e7aa;
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>2. Ensure a Root Wrapper</strong></p>
<p>For <code>::deep</code> to work, the elements you are targeting must be descendants of an element that the CSS isolation mechanism &quot;recognizes.&quot; If a MudBlazor component is the very first thing in your file, it might not have the isolation identifier.</p>
<p>Wrap your code in a div or use the MudPaper as the anchor:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class=&quot;my-custom-container&quot;&gt;
    &lt;MudPaper ...&gt;
        &lt;/MudPaper&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Note: If you use a <code>div</code> wrapper, the CSS should ideally look like this: <code>.my-custom-container ::deep .rounded-pill</code>. This ensures the scope is correctly identified.</p>
